            "review_text": "YY6128\nSingapore, Singapore69 contributions\n0\nGood quality food, justified by it's price tag\nSep 2015 • Friends\nVisited this place with certain level of expectation, and was not disappointed. Service was good, wonderful ambience with neat food presentation. Fresh ingredients were used, vegetables were crisp and offered great compliments to the charcoal grilled meats. \nMeats were well marinated, without covering the freshness of the pork used. Seafood used for the soup were probably sourced from market, and was as fresh as it gets. \nAll in all a great experience, but of course, have to be prepared to fork out alittle more for food in such area, as well as the quality offered (a good USD60/ pax).\nRead more\nWritten September 17, 2015",
